  "title": "Talking to Your Team About Prevention",
  "summary": "Starting conversations about needlestick safety without blame or assumptions Needlestick injuries continue to affect healthcare workers across the United States, even after decades of regulation and the widespread adoption of safety-engineered devices. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention estimates that approximately 385,000 needlestick and other sharps injuries occur each year among hospital-based healthcare personnel. […]",
